# `docker/Dockerfile` does `COPY . .` into the build stage.
#
# Without this file, MASTER_KEY and every encrypted attachment on the host end
# up in the image's build layers — readable by anyone who can pull it, and
# needed by nothing: the build gets its placeholders from the Dockerfile and its
# real configuration from compose at runtime.
#
# It also stops the host's node_modules landing on top of the ones the deps
# stage just installed, which is how a native module built for the host libc
# ends up inside a Debian image.
.env
.env.*
.env.example

data/
uploads/
*.pgdump

node_modules/
.next/
.git/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
